# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]   (no dollar/backtick in the text)
register_gate "tests/test_graph_insights_reader.py" "GRAPH-INSIGHTS READER GATE: PASS" "graph insights reader" "the hosted platform dashboard can read a SPECIFIC installation's ALWAYS-PRESENT structural intelligence content-free: core.graph_insights_for_installation(text[, repo]) resolves the installation to its account, picks the BUSIEST repo (most code_node rows, on the branch with the most nodes) OR -- with the optional repo arg -- the SPECIFIC repo being viewed (only if it is one of the account's OWN repos, else benign empty), and returns the customer's OWN top co-change couplings (lift>=2 AND co>=3, a<b, pct=round(strength*100)) plus the most-depended-on files (in-repo import fan-in = COUNT DISTINCT code_edge.src over imports edges resolved to internal file nodes) -- so the dashboard is NO LONGER dead when there are no recent collisions (every other reader read is collision-event based) and the per-repo detail page shows the same graph scoped to its repo. It NEVER exposes node/edge totals, the coverage % / billing metric, or cross-account data, and NEVER raises (empty/unknown/blank id, or a repo not belonging to the account -> the benign {repo:null,coupled:[],central:[]})" "Adds the always-present graph-insights reader (additive; mirrors account_coverage_for_installation exactly -- SECURITY DEFINER, OWNER veripsa_migrator, routed installation->account pin so RLS scopes every read to one tenant, REVOKE PUBLIC + GRANT EXECUTE to example_platform_reader + veripsa_app) with an OPTIONAL second arg p_repo (DEFAULT NULL -> the prior busiest-repo behavior, so the 1-arg call site is unchanged; a given repo is scoped ONLY if it is one of the account's own repos, validated by a code_node membership check under the account pin, else benign empty -- never another tenant's data). Closes the dead-dashboard gap: effect/now/repo_insights are all collision-event based, so the customer console goes dark with no recent contention even though the code graph + co-change cache are full. This read projects that standing structure content-free: file PATHS (already stored), a co-change % (strength -- the same figure the PR-check coverage-nudge/cochange already render), and an in-repo dependents COUNT of the customer's own files. The gate stands up the ephemeral Postgres + a fixture (ACCT-DEMO inst 111: a busiest repo with file/def nodes, a DECOY repo with fewer nodes, a NON-busiest svc-repo with its own graph + coupling, import edges incl. a duplicate src and an external/no-file-node target, and 4 co-change pairs -- 2 above the lift>=2/co>=3 floor, 2 below; an EMPTY tenant ACCT-EMPTY inst 333 with no graph but owning a FOREIGN repo) and proves live: (1) the busiest repo is picked, coupled = exactly the 2 floor-passing pairs ranked lift-desc with a<b and pct, central files ranked by DISTINCT-importer fan-in (the duplicate edge does not double-count, the external target is dropped); (2) content-free -- a forbidden body/secret marker seeded as node names + a dropped import target NEVER appears, every string leaf is an expected file path; (3) the example_platform_reader role CAN EXECUTE it and gets the same shape (has_function_privilege true for reader + app, false for a buyer/seat class -- PUBLIC revoked); (4) graceful empty -- no-graph / unknown / blank / null id all return the benign empty shape; (5) per-repo scope -- p_repo=NULL/1-arg are byte-identical to the busiest repo, a NON-busiest repo of the account returns ITS OWN coupled/central (the busiest repo does not bleed in), and a repo NOT belonging to the account (another tenant's, or unknown) returns the benign empty shape with content-free intact. Content-free (paths/counts/pct only)." 30
